  "def_titan_rare_desc": "Titan-50 is a rare ore containing the heavier isotope of common titanium.\r\n\r\n''Isotopes and variants have different levels of purity. The more pure this strange mineral is, the more common minerals can be [[Help:Recycling_items|recycled]] from it. Purity levels range from PL-10 to PL-90.''\r\n\r\n''Note that variants appear randomly, during the exploitation of [[Help:Raw_materials|common]] minerals. There's no way to detect them directly.''\n  ",
  "def_crude_rare_desc": "Its slightly expanded molecular structure makes H2DT an excellent, versatile organic energy source.\r\n\r\n''Isotopes and variants have different levels of purity. The more pure this strange mineral is, the more common minerals can be [[Help:Recycling_items|recycled]] from it. Purity levels range from PL-10 to PL-90.''\r\n\r\n''Note that variants appear randomly, during the exploitation of [[Help:Raw_materials|common]] minerals. There's no way to detect them directly.''\n  ",
  "def_stermonit_rare_desc": "Extraordinary pressure and heat forged the common stermonit into an exceptionally pure crystal.\r\n\r\n''Isotopes and variants have different levels of purity. The more pure this strange mineral is, the more common minerals can be [[Help:Recycling_items|recycled]] from it. Purity levels range from PL-10 to PL-90.''\r\n\r\n''Note that variants appear randomly, during the exploitation of [[Help:Raw_materials|common]] minerals. There's no way to detect them directly.''\n  ",
  "def_imentium_rare_desc": "Due to its special crystal structure, useful minerals are located more densely, than in the common imentium ore.\r\n\r\n''Isotopes and variants have different levels of purity. The more pure this strange mineral is, the more common minerals can be [[Help:Recycling_items|recycled]] from it. Purity levels range from PL-10 to PL-90.''\r\n\r\n''Note that variants appear randomly, during the exploitation of [[Help:Raw_materials|common]] minerals. There's no way to detect them directly.''\n  ",
  "def_liquizit_rare_desc": "This versatile, but fairly unstable metal consists of three liquizit molecules merged together.\r\n\r\n''Isotopes and variants have different levels of purity. The more pure this strange mineral is, the more common minerals can be [[Help:Recycling_items|recycled]] from it. Purity levels range from PL-10 to PL-90.''\r\n\r\n''Note that variants appear randomly, during the exploitation of [[Help:Raw_materials|common]] minerals. There's no way to detect them directly.''\n  ",
  "def_epriton_rare_desc": "Compared to common epriton, the special dyrepriton consists of 3 different metals, but the mineral conserved its useful abilities.\r\n\r\n''Isotopes and variants have different levels of purity. The more pure this strange mineral is, the more common minerals can be [[Help:Recycling_items|recycled]] from it. Purity levels range from PL-10 to PL-90.''\r\n\r\n''Note that variants appear randomly, during the exploitation of [[Help:Raw_materials|common]] minerals. There's no way to detect them directly.''\n  ",
  "def_helioptris_rare_desc": "At the final stage of the harvesting process, the harvester module slightly compresses the extruded material, sometimes causing the solid starch to transform into helioquid.\r\n\r\n''Isotopes and variants have different levels of purity. The more pure this strange mineral is, the more common minerals can be [[Help:Recycling_items|recycled]] from it. Purity levels range from PL-10 to PL-90.''\r\n\r\n''Note that variants appear randomly, during the exploitation of [[Help:Raw_materials|common]] minerals. There's no way to detect them directly.''\n  ",
  "def_triandlus_rare_desc": "During a long natural process, the triandlus can transform into a more dense material, tricarine. The radiation caused by the harvester module can sometimes artificially speed up the process.\r\n\r\n''Isotopes and variants have different levels of purity. The more pure this strange mineral is, the more common minerals can be [[Help:Recycling_items|recycled]] from it. Purity levels range from PL-10 to PL-90.''\r\n\r\n''Note that variants appear randomly, during the exploitation of [[Help:Raw_materials|common]] minerals. There's no way to detect them directly.''\n  ",
  "def_electroplant_fruit_rare_desc": "As a result of the incubation technology's constant and excessive nutrition, parts of the noralgis plant can aggregate, leaving an organic variant, Noralgae behind.\r\n\r\n''Isotopes and variants have different levels of purity. The more pure this strange mineral is, the more common minerals can be [[Help:Recycling_items|recycled]] from it. Purity levels range from PL-10 to PL-90.''\r\n\r\n''Note that variants appear randomly, during the exploitation of [[Help:Raw_materials|common]] minerals. There's no way to detect them directly.''\n  ",
