  "def_redeemable_credit_dlc0": "4,800 Perpetuum Credits\n  ",
  "def_redeemable_credit_dlc1": "2,500 Perpetuum Credits\n  ",
  "def_redeemable_spark_dlc0": "Solaris ST1 \"Yuge\" spark\n  ",
  "def_redeemable_spark_dlc1": "Matsuda Suchimu Type-S spark\n  ",
  "error_SparkAlreadyUnlocked": "This spark has been already redeemed for this character. Please select another!\n  ",
  "accounttransactiontype_creditredeem": "Credit redeem\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_advanced_artifacts_trigger04_desc": "Artifacts pop up in similar containers like loot, so just double-click to open them and take their contents.\r\n\r\nThis marks the end of this chapter. The fourth and final chapter starts again in the terminal, so take the teleport back and enter.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_refining_trigger01_desc": "Raw materials that you mine or harvest need to be refined in order to be used in production.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_refining_trigger02_desc": "You can select which refined commodity you want to create from the '''dropdown menu'''. Type the amount you want to create, and the required amount of raw materials will be displayed on the left.\r\n\r\nSome raw minerals, like titan ore, can be directly refined into a commodity. However, most of the commodities need to be created with a combination of two or more materials.\r\n\r\n[[Image:checklist_refine.jpg|center|nolink]]\r\nRefining happens instantly, you just have to click the '''create button'''. We have sent a stack of titan ore into your private storage, go ahead and refine some.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_recycling_trigger01_desc": "Commodities can also be created by recycling equipment that you don't need.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_recycling_trigger02_desc": "If you open the '''Recycling plant''', it will list all the equipment in your storage that can be recycled. Select the items you want to recycle using the '''checkboxes''', and the amounts you would get by recycling them will be shown on the right. Like refining, recycling also happens instantly.\r\n\r\n[[Image:checklist_recycle.jpg|center|nolink]]\r\n''Tip: you can also directly select items to recycle if you right-click them in your storage and select \"Recycle\". (Works on multiple selected items too.)''\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_research_trigger01_desc": "Now you know how to acquire the materials to build something, but you also need the knowledge. This happens by researching the appropriate '''technology'''.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_research_trigger02_desc": "All the technology that you can research is organized into a number of '''technology trees'''. Research needs to start from a '''root item''', and from there you can work your way towards more advanced items to the right.\r\n\r\nThe research process looks like this:\r\n[[Image:checklist_kernel.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\n* Researching an item requires '''Research Points (RP)'''.\r\n* RP can be acquired by researching '''kernels'''. They are dropped as loot by enemy robots, and they can also be found in some artifacts.\r\n* Different technologies require different types of RP, which are mostly tied to a faction. For example looting Pelistal (green) robots will give you Pelistal kernels, and researching them will yield Pelistal RP. Your available RP of each type is shown on the top.\r\n\r\nWe have sent a couple of '''Common kernels''' into your private storage. These kernels are dropped by all the factions. Research them to get some common RP.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_research_trigger03_desc": "One kernel equals 1 RP of the appropriate type, simple as that. Now that you have some RP, let's find some tech that you can unlock.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_research_trigger04_desc": "[[Image:checklist_research.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nYou should have enough common RP to unlock the Standard light autocannon that's located in the first column on the Common I page. (You might have to scroll down a bit to see it.)\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_research_trigger05_desc": "Researching an item enables you to unlock the items connected to it, if you have enough RP of course. Move on to the next task to see what you can do with this newly acquired knowledge.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_prototyping_trigger01_desc": "So now that you have the technology, you can create a prototype. Prototyping is very '''expensive''', but you only need one to create many copies of it via mass production.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_prototyping_trigger02_desc": "[[Image:checklist_prototype.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nOn the left you'll see all your known technology that you have unlocked via research. Select the '''Standard light autocannon''' and on the right you'll see what commodities you need to build it. We have sent a good bunch of Titanium and Axicoline to your storage so you don't have to worry about that now.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_reverseengineering_trigger01_desc": "Reverse engineering is used to create '''Calibration Templates (CTs)''' by studying prototypes. CTs are basically \"recipes\" for mass production, we use them to calibrate our factory production lines to manufacture a specific item.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_prototyping_trigger03_desc": "The process will '''take some time''', depending on your extensions, the facility itself, and the type of the item. In the interest of time, industrial processes are vastly sped up during this virtual training.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_reverseengineering_trigger02_desc": "In order to reverse engineer something, you need an item (usually a prototype) and a '''decoder''' of the required level. Like kernels, decoders can be acquired from enemy loot or artifacts. Both the item and the decoder are '''consumed''' during the process.\r\n\r\nThe prototyping of your standard autocannon should be finished by now, so drag it into the reverse engineering window. We have sent an extra autocannon to your storage too, just in case.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_reverseengineering_trigger03_desc": "We've also sent you a decoder, drag that one in too.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_reverseengineering_trigger04_desc": "[[Image:checklist_reverseengineer.jpg|center|nolink]]\r\nBefore you start the process you can check the quality of the resulting CT. Higher '''material efficiency''' means that you will need less materials to mass produce this item, and a higher '''time efficiency''' means that it will take less time.\r\n\r\n''Tip: if you have a higher level decoder than what's required, you can use it instead to achieve a higher quality CT and reduce the time and cost of the reverse engineering process.''\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_reverseengineering_trigger05_desc": "''Note: normally you don't need to create prototypes of \"standard\" items, because they can be used directly in reverse engineering. Only higher tier equipment and robots need to be prototyped.''\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_massproduction_trigger01_desc": "The factory is the final stage of the production chain, this is where mass production happens.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_massproduction_trigger02_desc": "[[Image:checklist_ct.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nYou have a number of '''production lines''' available here, which can be '''calibrated''' to produce items by applying CTs to them. '''Wait''' until the reverse engineering process that you have started is finished (if it's still running), and then drag the created CT into the factory.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_massproduction_trigger03_desc": "[[Image:checklist_factory.jpg|center|nolink]]\r\nSelect the calibrated production line and you'll see the required materials to manufacture it, just like in the prototype facility. Since this is mass production, you will usually do more than one '''manufacturing cycle''', so you can input that here as well, and the required material amounts will be automatically updated. For now though, one autocannon will be enough.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_massproduction_trigger04_desc": "Note that every production cycle will '''degrade''' the calibration and decrease its efficiency. A line with low efficiency will require increasingly '''more materials''' and will take more time to produce something, so eventually the point will come where it's not worth to use it anymore. When this happens, you can delete the calibration from the line's right-click menu and apply a new CT created in reverse engineering.\r\n\r\nThis is all you need to know about the industry for now. '''Move on to the next task''' and we'll do some shooting again, this time with something bigger.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_thelodicarobots_trigger01_desc": "[[Image:checklist_artemis.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nTo be fair, this will be a bit teasing. The '''mech-class''' robots you’re about to try won’t be available to you from the start, you will have to work for them. But it’s important that you get a good impression about the different factions, so you can make a choice without regrets.\r\n\r\nThe first one you’re going to test is the '''Artemis'''. It’s a mech of the Thelodica faction, who are specialized in '''laser weaponry'''.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_thelodicarobots_trigger02_desc": "It’s equipped with a few interesting modules that we’ll also try out, so let’s jump outside.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_thelodicarobots_trigger03_desc": "[[Image:checklist_artemisbonus.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nAll robots have certain special '''bonuses''' which make them excel in certain fields. You can take a look at these bonuses if you bring up the information window of your robot (the blue i icon on your robot status panel), and click the bonuses tab.\r\n\r\nThe Artemis receives bonuses to its armor resistance values. The damage output of all weapons is a combination of four possible '''damage types''': kinetic, thermal, seismic, or chemical. Armor resistance will, as the name says, resist a percentage of the appropriate incoming damage type.\r\n\r\nSo this mech already has a good base of resists, but we can top that in order to receive as little damage as possible. There are two types of modules for this purpose: active and passive armors.\r\n\r\n[[Image:checklist_armors.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\n'''Active armors''', like the equipped seismic and thermal armors give large resistance boosts for a specific damage type, but they have to be activated and use some energy. The '''universal armor''' (also equipped on your robot) is a passive module, you just need to equip it and it does its thing. It provides resistance boosts to all four damage types, but only small amounts for each.\r\n\r\nActivate the seismic armor module, and you’ll see that its effect icon will appear under your robot status panel. All active effects that boost or harm your robot in any way will appear here. Hover over them with your mouse to get more information.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_thelodicarobots_trigger04_desc": "The main advantage of lasers is their relatively '''large range''', and that they are more '''precise''' when hitting smaller targets than other weapon types.\r\n\r\n[[Image:checklist_sensoramp.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nHowever, a large weapon range is only good if you can lock a target that far. This is when a '''sensor amplifier''' can come in handy, which not only boosts your robot’s locking range, but also the time it needs to lock targets. It’s an active module as well, but only uses a low amount of energy to operate.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_thelodicarobots_trigger05_desc": "''Tip: logically, it’s always optimal to have a locking range that is larger than your weapons’ range. You can compare these if you check the information panels of your robot and your weapon modules.''\r\n\r\nAlright that’s enough talk, let’s head to the '''shooting range'''.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_thelodicarobots_trigger06_desc": "Note that your active modules are turned off by the teleport, so you will need to activate them again to make them work.\r\n\r\nWell, you know the drill, primary lock a '''Drone''' and destroy it. The task will complete after one kill already, but feel free to stay around and do some more shooting to get a feel for it.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_thelodicarobots_trigger07_desc": "Head back to the terminal when you’re done, the '''next mech''' already awaits you.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_pelistalrobots_trigger01_desc": "[[Image:checklist_tyrannos.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nYou might have noticed that the Artemis didn’t only have lasers, but one missile launcher as well. This is the case for all mechs, they are using a mixed set of weapons to be versatile.\r\n\r\nThe next robot actually uses '''missiles''' as primary weapons, with guns as secondary armament. This is the '''Tyrannos''', the mech of the ballistics-specialist Pelistal faction.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_pelistalrobots_trigger02_desc": "Missiles are quite different compared to guns, because they '''shoot in an arc''' instead of a straight line. This makes it possible to attack something even from behind cover. Let’s deploy and see how this works in practice.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_pelistalrobots_trigger03_desc": "[[Image:checklist_missiles.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nAnother peculiar trait of missiles is that unlike guns, which have short and long range versions, the range difference here lies in the loaded ammo. This allows you to be effective at both '''short and long ranges''', you just have to switch to the appropriate missiles. There should be a few of both types in your cargo, feel free to change them if you want.\r\n\r\nLet’s hit the '''shooting range''' again.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_pelistalrobots_trigger04_desc": "The Tyrannos gets a bonus for its accumulator recharge time, and we have even boosted this by equipping an '''accumulator recharger''' and an '''auxiliary accumulator''' module. Why do we need so much energy? Because we also have a shield generator module.\r\n\r\n[[Image:checklist_shield.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nWhen your '''shield''' is active, it will perfectly deflect enemy fire. To be able to do this however, it will use energy from your robot’s accumulator - the more damage, the more energy used. So effectively your accumulator becomes your second armor, as long as it has energy to consume.\r\n\r\nLet’s lock a Drone to get its attention, but '''don’t shoot it just yet'''.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_pelistalrobots_trigger05_desc": "Now activate your shield generator and watch how the bullets get deflected by it.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_pelistalrobots_trigger06_desc": "Sadly there is always a catch: shields deflect shots from both sides, so you '''can’t fire''' your weapons while your shield is active. '''Deactivate''' your shield and kill any attacking drones so they won’t bother you anymore.\r\n\r\n[[Image:checklist_shootscarab.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nSo remember that missiles can shoot over things? There is a bunch of '''Hauler drones''' nearby which are enclosed by a tall fence. Go ahead and try to kill one with your machine guns only - you’ll probably won’t succeed and only hit the walls.\r\n\r\nThe only way to kill one is by using your missiles from the proper distance. Let’s see if you can do that.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_pelistalrobots_trigger07_desc": "Great, you’re getting the hang of this. Kill some more if you like and then return to the terminal again for the '''last mech'''.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_nuimqolrobots_trigger01_desc": "[[Image:checklist_kain.jpg|right|nolink]]\r\nThe last mech we’ll show you is the Nuimqol faction’s '''Kain'''. This faction specializes in '''magnetic weaponry''', which have a relatively short range, but the sheer damage they can deal makes up for it.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_nuimqolrobots_trigger02_desc": "This mech also has a few interesting modules equipped, let’s deploy and we’ll have a look at them.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_nuimqolrobots_trigger03_desc": "'''Speed''' is one of the key aspects of combat. If you’re faster than your enemy, you can easily catch up to your prey, but you also have a higher chance of escaping from a tight situation.\r\n\r\n[[Image:mass_reductor.png|right|nolink]]\r\nThe Kain is already the fastest of the three mechs, but we have even topped that by equipping a '''lightweight frame'''. This module increases your speed by making your robot lighter, but it also reduces its armor. Good thing that one of the Kain’s bonuses is boosting armor repair, which is further supported by the armor repairer tuning module. The evasive module makes your robot harder to hit, and an active armor is added to compensate the Kain’s weakest resistance, thermal.\r\n\r\nLet’s head to the '''shooting range''' once again and see what it can do.\n  ",
  "tutorialchecklist_complex_nuimqolrobots_trigger04_desc": "There is not much left to say really. Lock on and light up those gauss guns!\n  ",
  "mission_tutorialchecklist_transport_desc": "This assignment is about the pickup and delivery of a larger package.\r\n\r\nThere are three objectives, marked [color=#00d8ff][b]A[/b][/color], [color=#00d8ff][b]B[/b][/color], and [color=#00d8ff][b]C[/b][/color]:\r\n\r\n[color=#00d8ff][b]Objective A[/b][/color] is a \"reach position\" type, you simply have to move to the objective point.\r\n\r\n[color=#00d8ff][b]Objective B[/b][/color] needs you to activate the [color=#ffffff][b]Item supply[/b][/color] object by double clicking on it. The process takes a little time, if you move it will get interrupted. When it's completed, the package will be placed into your cargo.\r\n\r\n[color=#00d8ff][b]Objective C[/b][/color] marks where you need to drop off the package. Move close to that location, and double click on the [color=#ffffff][b]Item delivery[/b][/color] object to open it. Then open your cargo and drag the Synsec container over into the \"Submit items\" window.\r\n\r\nWhen all objectives are done, the assignment is complete.\n  ",
  "welcomescreen_text_4realz": "This is it. The real Nia.\r\n\r\nYou're now an integral part of the Perpetuum Project and from now on your actions have consequences.\r\n\r\nUse what you have learnt during your training and establish yourself in this new world. Keep on learning, there is much more to know.\r\n\r\nStart a career in the industry or get on the frontlines.\r\nComplete assignments or go out exploring.\r\nBe a lone wolf or join a corporation.\r\n\r\nIt's up to you.\r\n\r\nGood luck, Agent.\n  ",
